linuxfs P3 bundle: the product's CLI, root helper and automount agent on Mac OS X 10.9.

Needs: Mavergreen macFUSE installed (lklfuse loads /usr/local/lib/libfuse3.4.dylib). No network, python or root
login. Copy this directory to the guest's local disk and, as the user logged in at the console:

    cd ~/linuxfs-p3-N && sh run.sh

Part A (CLI on images) runs as that user. Part B installs and loads the root helper with `sudo -n`; without
passwordless sudo it is skipped. The helper stays loaded through Part C, as an installed agent probes disks
through it, and is unloaded and removed at the end. Part C (the automount agent) needs the user logged in at the
console (Finder running) and the helper; without them it is skipped. Its images are attached -nomount, so
DiskArbitration peeks at them (the agent claims and mounts) but mounts nothing itself; whether the Mac's "not
readable" dialog would appear needs a real disk, so it is not asked. Last, Part C attaches an encrypted APFS
image: a dialog "Unlock an encrypted volume" appears on the console. Enter linuxfs-test, tick "Remember this
password in my keychain", and press Mount (there are three minutes; unanswered, that step is skipped). It is
ejected (the disk must go, and the agent log that it kept the password), then attached once more and should mount from the keychain with no second dialog: please say whether one appeared.
With no one at the screen (over ssh), run `P3_ASKPASS=1 sh run.sh`: a script answers in place of the dialog, and
the second attach is checked to ask nothing; the dialog itself is then left untested.

The guest is left as it was found, on any exit, a failed one included: the helper (loaded without -w, so
launchd's overrides are untouched), its log (copied to out/), any linuxfs mount this run made still up, any of
the run's images still attached, new empty mount points in /Volumes, the keychain items filed under the test
image's partition, the dev.mavergreen.linuxfs preferences (restored as they were, or removed when there were
none), and work/ (its raw images; its small files, errors and logs, are kept in out/work/).

Send back: results.txt and the out/ directory (images and logs).
